# DEV_CONTAINER_NAME for bin/ckCommon: names a persistent container (created
# once via `bin/dockerRun <image> <name>`) that the docker backend
# (_docker_run_local) reuses via `docker exec` instead of spinning up a fresh
# --rm container per command, when that container is currently running.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/ckdevcontainer (or point DEV_CONTAINER_NAME_FILE
# elsewhere) to enable. Missing file (the default): no reuse, every command
# runs in a fresh --rm container as before.
#
# Reuse ignores DOCKER_SETUP_CMD entirely — keeping this container's setup in
# sync with DOCKER_SETUP_CMD is on you, not something this flow reconciles.
# Only a RUNNING container is reused; a stopped one falls back to the normal
# --rm flow (dockerRun's --restart=always should keep it running regardless).
#
# File content is just the container name, nothing else:
my_dev_container
